{
  "about": "Where held items sit. Held_Offset_R_Transform and Held_Offset_L_Transform are the offsets of an item held in the right or left hand, from that hand's bone (hand.R, hand.L); an item in a hand uses that offset. An item's own Held_Item_Offset_Transform further offsets it from the hand offset (it is applied after the hand offset, in the hand's frame). Raised_Held_Item_Offset_Transform is the same for an item that is raised (a shield, while Q is held). A transform is position (blocks), rotation (degrees: X, then Y, then Z, applied as Rz * Ry * Rx) and scale. An item with \"bone\" is attached to that bone of its hand's model instead (a shield on the forearm), and then the hand offset is not used.",
